    "summary": "Added the pure \u00a76 encounter rules as @pirate-sea-race/simulation/encounters (geometry.ts: supercover LOS, bearing by max dot product, circular cones, squared ranges; modes.ts: full sea rules + foot placeholder; state.ts: config/state/events/markers; step.ts: stepEncounters/replayEncounters) and the tuning as @pirate-sea-race/content/encounters (constants in seconds converted to ticks, zod validator). One subpath export added to each of packages/simulation/package.json and packages/content/package.json (source condition first); no postbuild, dependency, barrel or tsconfig changed. Tests: content validator test (negative duration, range above sight radius), geometry tests (supercover equals an exact rational reference on all 6561 pairs of a 9x9 grid, both directions; land blocks, shoals do not; \u00b14/\u00b18 cone boundaries; exact squared-range boundary), 43 scripted rule tests, and seeded property tests over the slice sea and three synthetic maps (40 seeds x 1600 ticks: invariants every tick, replay hash equality, EXERCISED coverage of every event kind and reason, input reorder and two order-preserving relabellings). docs/encounters.md written. Executed locally after npm ci: npm run typecheck (exit 0), npm run test:unit (684 passed), npm run test:integration (37 passed), npm run build (exit 0, smoke passed); also imported both new subpaths from dist/ by hand.",
